Apply one controller HTTP policy to HTTP, TLS, Unix and named-pipe listeners.

Use a shared constructor: ReadHeaderTimeout 15 seconds, IdleTimeout 2 minutes,
MaxHeaderBytes 256 KiB, and no overall ReadTimeout or WriteTimeout for streams.

Regression tests exercise real HTTP/TLS serving over net.Pipe. They observe the
production deadlines before shortening only the test connection's waiting time.
Cover incomplete headers, a stalled TLS handshake, idle keep-alive, accepted and
oversized headers, a slow request body and a delayed streaming response.
No IP-bound listeners or certificate/private-key files are used by the tests.

